ating, inflationary e-fold matching, and possible oscillon instabilities?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:478ba2c9dbfcca0975461d30b71b4f59f7180e1cc3848bcc8325d69d5c66ed5c","title":"How sensitive are scalar-gravity fixed points and their relevant directions to regulator dependence and anomalous-dimension prescriptions? The appendix distinguishes scalar, metric-fluctuation, and background Newton-coupling anomalous dimensions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:475b0799a230ee1832e432eb331e11d02dffcc2538ae16754a1c7adff77cc8e6","title":"Can flux changes permit arbitrarily many space-time filling branes, and therefore arbitrarily large gauge rank, while retaining fixed compactification and orientifold data?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:47f7a67ce6a2cf81a3163b2142ecc40357ae05bf695e27957a34f27ba3c507bc","title":"Can reinforcement learning and genetic algorithms efficiently locate rare phenomenologically attractive heterotic monad models in spaces too large for systematic scans, and how complete are their searches on the chosen Calabi–Yau examples?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:47ad085d52785da87279f006ada4645906960d46c308c590478b557800895c4c","title":"When do discrete theta angles define physically distinct quantum gravities with identical massless supergravity, and how do they change massive spectra, dualities and BPS completeness in compactifications with sixteen supercharges?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:47443fae7ca15a69a548c8f095ef34d47a7ba9af4e19f55eda91d95039831b99","title":